<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00RB">Remark <span data-tag="00RB">2.5.6.20</span>.</a> Let $A_{\bullet }$ be a simplicial abelian group. Then Warning <a data-tag="00RA" href="/tag/00RA">2.5.6.19</a> supplies a canonical isomorphism of normalized Moore complexes $\mathrm{N}_{\ast }(A) \simeq \mathrm{N}_{\ast }( A^{\operatorname{op}} )$. By virtue of Theorem <a data-tag="00QR" href="/tag/00QR">2.5.6.1</a>, this isomorphism can be lifted uniquely to an isomorphism of simplicial abelian groups $\varphi : A_{\bullet } \simeq A_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{op}}$. The isomorphism $\varphi $ is characterized by the requirement that for every $n$-simplex $x \in A_ n$, we have $\varphi (x) \equiv (-1)^{\frac{n^2+n}{2}} x$ modulo degenerate simplices of $A_{\bullet }$. </p>
